 slurs are represented with two elements: one with a start type, and one with a stop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type. Slurs can add more elements using a continue type. This is typically used to specify the formatting of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cross-system slurs, or to specify the shape of very complex slurs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur"}}}